{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Let the earth bring forth grass, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory (Ḥullin 60a) said that although the Creator did not say ״לְמִינוֹ״ (after its kind) except for the tree, the grasses extrapolated a fortiori, etc. And it is difficult, for according to the order of the verse HaShem preceded His words concerning the grasses, and if so, why were they delayed from sprouting immediately, right next to HaShem's utterance, until HaShem finished saying to bring forth the tree, from which they extrapolated a fortiori? And according to what I explained in the verse ״בְּרֵאשִׁית״ — that every place where a matter of might is spoken in the name Elohim, He speaks the entire statement in a single utterance — if so, there was no precedence of the grasses before the tree."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:55:04.931660598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}